    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d714">

                <pb facs="0931" n="921" sameAs="frus:frus1947v07/pg921"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.24/11–647: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Stuart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-11-19T16:00:00-05:00">November 19,
                            1947—4 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1401. Following is Secy’s reply for safehandling to FonMin (Your unnumbered [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">No. 2200</hi>] tel Nov 6, 1 p.m.): <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Dear Dr. Wang: Before leaving for London I wish to thank you for the
                            letter which you gave Amb Stuart for transmission to me. No doubt Amb
                            Koo has already reported to you the substance of our conversation on
                            Nov. 13,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d714-f1"/> in the course of which I
                            supplied him with background information in regard to the proposed
                            assistance for China which I set forth in broad outline to the
                            Congressional Committees last week.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d714-f2"/> I
                            particularly want you to know, as I told Amb Koo, that we are seeking to
                            determine what ammunition suitable for Chinese needs may be available in
                            the Marianas and expect further to communicate with you on the subject
                            as soon as it is possible. Dr. Koo will have informed you, I am sure, of
                            my views as to the undesirability of publicity with respect to this
                            matter.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
